WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.141
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.441 --> 00:00:08.595
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.895 --> 00:00:16.110
Unit sixteen: Life After School. Today you will talk about future plans in progress with the future continuous.

4
00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.109
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:23.880
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:24.717 --> 00:00:25.845
Transition.

7
00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:30.138
Transition means a change from one stage to another.

8
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.411
The transition to university can be hard.

9
00:00:34.017 --> 00:00:36.797
Your turn. Say: Transition.

10
00:00:39.633 --> 00:00:40.634
Transition.

11
00:00:41.383 --> 00:00:42.826
Higher education.

12
00:00:43.817 --> 00:00:47.117
Higher education means study at university or college.

13
00:00:47.717 --> 00:00:50.320
Higher education opens many doors.

14
00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:54.184
Your turn. Say: Higher education.

15
00:00:57.033 --> 00:00:58.336
Higher education.

16
00:00:59.083 --> 00:01:00.444
Vocational training.

17
00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:04.773
Vocational training means training for a practical job.

18
00:01:05.383 --> 00:01:08.021
He chose vocational training in electrics.

19
00:01:08.617 --> 00:01:11.455
Your turn. Say: Vocational training.

20
00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.882
Vocational training.

21
00:01:16.617 --> 00:01:17.536
Gap year.

22
00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:22.326
Gap year means a year off between school and university.

23
00:01:22.917 --> 00:01:25.090
She volunteered during her gap year.

24
00:01:25.683 --> 00:01:27.894
Your turn. Say: Gap year.

25
00:01:30.733 --> 00:01:31.792
Gap year.

26
00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:33.807
Independence.

27
00:01:34.817 --> 00:01:37.919
Independence means living and deciding for yourself.

28
00:01:38.517 --> 00:01:40.923
Moving to the city gave me independence.

29
00:01:41.517 --> 00:01:44.273
Your turn. Say: Independence.

30
00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:48.309
Independence.

31
00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:50.214
Life skill.

32
00:01:51.217 --> 00:01:54.157
Life skill means a skill you need for daily life.

33
00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:56.889
Cooking is a useful life skill.

34
00:01:57.483 --> 00:02:00.809
Your turn. Say: Life skill.

35
00:02:03.667 --> 00:02:05.167
Life skill.

36
00:02:05.917 --> 00:02:07.336
Career readiness.

37
00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:11.104
Career readiness means being prepared for work.

38
00:02:11.717 --> 00:02:14.076
Internships build career readiness.

39
00:02:14.683 --> 00:02:17.835
Your turn. Say: Career readiness.

40
00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:22.107
Career readiness.

41
00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:24.199
Self-sufficiency.

42
00:02:25.183 --> 00:02:28.147
Self-sufficiency means being able to look after yourself.

43
00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.411
Self-sufficiency means paying your own bills.

44
00:02:32.017 --> 00:02:34.982
Your turn. Say: Self-sufficiency.

45
00:02:37.833 --> 00:02:39.345
Self-sufficiency.

46
00:02:40.083 --> 00:02:41.154
Adulthood.

47
00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:44.602
Adulthood means the time of being an adult.

48
00:02:45.217 --> 00:02:47.785
Adulthood brings new responsibilities.

49
00:02:48.383 --> 00:02:51.140
Your turn. Say: Adulthood.

50
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.013
Adulthood.

51
00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:57.111
Decision-making.

52
00:02:58.117 --> 00:03:01.161
Decision-making means the process of making choices.

53
00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:03.947
Good decision-making takes time.

54
00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:07.864
Your turn. Say: Decision-making.

55
00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:12.189
Decision-making.

56
00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:14.276
Uncertainty.

57
00:03:15.283 --> 00:03:18.421
Uncertainty means not knowing what will happen.

58
00:03:19.017 --> 00:03:21.330
Uncertainty about the future is normal.

59
00:03:21.917 --> 00:03:24.372
Your turn. Say: Uncertainty.

60
00:03:27.233 --> 00:03:28.351
Uncertainty.

61
00:03:29.117 --> 00:03:30.211
Opportunity.

62
00:03:31.217 --> 00:03:33.971
Opportunity means a good chance to do something.

63
00:03:34.583 --> 00:03:37.140
University is a great opportunity.

64
00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.727
Your turn. Say: Opportunity.

65
00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:44.719
Opportunity.

66
00:03:45.533 --> 00:03:49.184
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:52.108
Visal, what will you be doing next year?

68
00:03:53.217 --> 00:03:56.842
Next year, I will be studying at university.

69
00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:59.195
Where will you be living?

70
00:04:00.283 --> 00:04:03.096
I will be living in Phnom Penh with my cousin.

71
00:04:04.183 --> 00:04:05.324
Are you nervous?

72
00:04:06.417 --> 00:04:11.368
A little. There is uncertainty, but it is a big opportunity.

73
00:04:12.533 --> 00:04:14.277
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:15.117 --> 00:04:17.476
Grammar focus: Future continuous.

75
00:04:17.776 --> 00:04:19.091
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:19.783 --> 00:04:22.398
Next year, I will be studying at university.

77
00:04:23.283 --> 00:04:26.281
This time next month, she will be working in a hotel.

78
00:04:27.183 --> 00:04:29.682
In September, we will be living in the city.

79
00:04:30.633 --> 00:04:35.326
Use the future continuous for an action that will be in progress at a time in the future.

80
00:04:36.083 --> 00:04:40.605
Be careful! Don't say: Next year, I will studying at university.

81
00:04:42.567 --> 00:04:45.994
Say: Next year, I will be studying at university.

82
00:04:46.294 --> 00:04:48.491
Future continuous is 'will be' + -ing.

83
00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.732
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:52.533 --> 00:04:53.813
The Next Chapter.

85
00:04:54.113 --> 00:04:56.426
Finishing school is a big transition.

86
00:04:57.433 --> 00:05:00.385
Some students will be going to higher education.

87
00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:05.071
Others will be doing vocational training or taking a gap year.

88
00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:09.007
Everyone will be learning life skills and independence.

89
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:13.010
Adulthood brings uncertainty, but also opportunity.

90
00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:18.218
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:19.083 --> 00:05:21.698
Next year, I will be blank at university.

92
00:05:21.998 --> 00:05:26.023
A, studying. B, study. C, studied.

93
00:05:29.567 --> 00:05:31.299
The answer is A: studying.

94
00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:35.634
A year off between school and university is a blank year.

95
00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:38.844
A, gap. B, life. C, free.

96
00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:43.842
The answer is A: gap.

97
00:05:44.983 --> 00:05:47.470
Training for a practical job is blank training.

98
00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:51.215
A, vocational. B, higher. C, career.

99
00:05:54.767 --> 00:05:56.917
The answer is A: vocational.

100
00:05:58.133 --> 00:06:01.088
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:05.378
What are you most excited or nervous about after finishing school?

102
00:06:14.183 --> 00:06:15.660
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:24.836
I am excited because I will be studying engineering. I am a little nervous about living alone, but I will be learning new life skills.

104
00:06:25.136 --> 00:06:26.926
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:27.817 --> 00:06:32.303
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and future continuous.

106
00:06:32.603 --> 00:06:37.369
Today's value is independence. Learn to do things by yourself, step by step.

107
00:06:37.669 --> 00:06:40.344
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

108
00:06:40.644 --> 00:06:43.366
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

